Description: Guidance for integrating with external APIs like AI services or search APIs.

Instructions: When calling external services (e.g., AnnasArchive, Gemini, Claude, OpenAI), implement the logic within a dedicated Service class (e.g., AnnasArchieve, GeminiService, ClaudeService, OpenAiService) in the data/ or domain/ layer of the relevant feature.

Implementation:Create a new Service class or modify an existing one.

Define methods for specific API interactions.

Handle request and response mapping.

Incorporate error handling and logging.

Integrate the service with the BLoC layer to manage state based on API responses (loading, success, error).

Context: Note the project's existing AI integrations and the conceptual RAG pipeline, with some RAG functionality currently handled in GeminiService.

Behavior: Ensure API interaction logic is encapsulated within services, keeping presentation logic separate. Use appropriate error handling and integrate results back into the application state via BLoCs.
